@startuml autonomous-product-relationships
title Autonomous Product Canonical Relationships ; per CR-ES-017 §6

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

class "Autonomous Product" as AP

class "Product" as P
class "Authority" as Auth
class "Policy" as Pol
class "Constraint" as Con
class "Objective" as Obj
class "Context" as Ctx
class "Outcome" as O
class "Workflow" as W
class "Agentic Workflow" as AW
class "Autonomous Operations" as AO
class "Capability" as Cap
class "Service" as S
class "Value" as V

AP --|> P : specializes
AP --> Auth : operates-within
AP --> Pol : governed-by
AP --> Con : constrained-by
AP --> Obj : pursues
AP --> Ctx : responds-to
AP --> O : produces
AP --> Ctx : adapts-to
AP --> W : uses (optional)
AP --> AW : uses (optional)
AP --> AO : supported-by
AP --> Cap : supports
AP --> S : delivered-through
AP --> V : contributes-to

note bottom of AP
  No foundational concept silently introduced per CR-ES-017 §6.
  Deferred concepts per ADR-ES-017 §14.
end note

@enduml
